    "notes": {
        "e2000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000ff01": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 160,
            "width": 560,
            "height": 240,
            "content": "**PR connector labels**\n\nEvery new pull request gets `appmixer:<connector>` for each connector whose files it changes — one label per `bundle.json`, plus `appmixer:google` / `appmixer:microsoft` / … for their shared root files. *Bundles on the PR head* and *Bundles on the PR base* read the `bundle.json` files at the PR's head and base commits, so a connector the PR adds or removes is labelled too, and nothing here has to be regenerated when a connector is added.\n\nA PR touching more than five connectors, or changing more than 100 files, gets no labels.\n\n**Add labels** needs **push** access: adding a label that does not exist yet creates it, which triage cannot.\n\n**Source of truth:** `.github/appmixer-flows/pr-connector-labels.json` in the connectors repo."
        }
    },
